(Stage 1e3 - nothing as a map value (tag 6) prints in place and is
 reachable via `is nothing`. A missing key stays an error (stage 1e2
 behavior unchanged): it sets the error flag and does NOT become nothing.
 Acceptance: the print line, the present-key predicate, and the
 missing-key error line.)

a map called "m" is {"k": nothing}.
print m.
if m's "k" is nothing, print "k is nothing".
if m's "missing" is nothing, print "missing is nothing (BUG)".
on error print "missing key errored".